{
 "id": "time_axis",
 "version": "1.2.0",
 "depends_on": [
  "shape_decode_loop"
 ],
 "description": "TIME AS AN INFERRED DIMENSION, ORDER-N. A sequence of frames presented in tick order is an ORBIT iff ONE transition generator G carries frame(t)->frame(t+1) for EVERY consecutive pair; that generator's exponent k IS the time axis, minted as a latent:time LatentDimension. The decision is the Rust TimeInfer Term (the temporal sibling of GenInfer, one level up): G is inferred from the first pair (affine translate preferred -- the retinal drifting-pattern case -- else integer 2x2 linear, the SAME enumerate-and-test as GenInfer) and VERIFIED by exact equality across every remaining pair (ORDER-1: constant velocity). When that exact-equality path GIVES UP -- the per-pair translate offset is itself CHANGING -- TimeInfer recurses with the DIMENSION-GENERIC finite-difference order-N mechanism (shape_decode.rs::diff_pyramid/pyramid_order): if the offset stream's finite differences reach a witnessed constant, it mints an ORDER-N generator (order 2 = acceleration, 3 = jerk, ...) carrying `order` + `coeffs` (the Newton forward coefficients). Only a stream that is NOT regular at any finite order (random) grounds unexplained -- the honest MDL floor, now placed at incompressibility rather than at order 1. The recursion is written over an ordered integer-vector stream with NO notion of which dimension indexes it, so the SAME code fits order-N along time, a spatial scan, or a minted latent axis. Time lives in Hom(frame,frame), never in a frame's coordinates (the frame/continuum invariant). Flag-gated on agent.time_infer_enabled==1, absent by default (OFF, PROTOCOL section 9); the whole seed is inert without it AND matches only status=='motion_seq' observations, which the normal decode ladder never produces.  v1.2.0 adds the FORWARD-PROJECTION reading of the same fit, on every path including the floor: `order_fit` (the order the stream's own generator was measured at) and `crossing` (how many steps that generator takes to carry the stream to its frame origin, capped at the caller's declared horizon -- a bound, never an order cap). `crossing` forced to order 1 is exactly margin/rate, the commonest quantity in any control loop wearing no clock; at the measured order it is a different number and the difference is the curvature the linear reading throws away. Materialised as TemporalProjection so consuming seeds can match on it. Domain-neutral by construction.",
 "microtheory": {
  "name": "time_axis",
  "description": "ordered motion orbit -> transition generator + latent:time dimension (+ downstream prediction of an unseen frame); a CHANGING-but-regular offset stream -> ORDER-N generator (velocity/acceleration/jerk...) via the dimension-generic finite-difference recursion; only an incompressible stream -> enumeration. Same operation as spatial generator discovery, applied to a temporal orbit and recursed to any order."
 },
